    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the skeleton of the trip: EV-TRIP-00212 records an 'arrived' event at 08:12:35, a wait_time_min of 7.9, a driver-initiated cancellation at 08:20:30 and the reason code EXCESSIVE_WAIT. That satisfies limbs (a) and (d) of POL-NS-01, and I accept it. But POL-NS-01 is conjunctive and the fee is chargeable only if all four limbs hold.\n\nLimb (b) fails. POL-NS-02 deems the driver to have arrived only where the GPS trace holds at least three consecutive fixes with horizontal accuracy of 25 m or better inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. On EV-GPS-00212 - COMPLETE, weight 1.0, 100% coverage, no gaps, 93 fixes - the derived arrival block reports 0 qualifying in-radius fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0 seconds. POL-NS-02 then provides in terms that where the trace contains no qualifying in-radius fix at any point in the 15 minutes before cancellation, the driver never arrived and the rider is entitled to a full refund. The driver's answer - that his near-pin fixes (min 37.94 m) were filtered out for poor accuracy, so the test proves nothing either way - is correct as to the filter but does not change the result. POL-NS-02 makes sub-25 m fixes count as evidence of neither presence nor absence precisely so that a low-accuracy reading cannot be used to establish arrival; it does not require the rider to prove the driver was outside the geofence. This trace is not impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d) - no skew, no sampling gap, more than 6 fixes, rider track present - so this is a test that ran and found nothing qualifying, not a test that could not be run.\n\nLimb (c) fails independently. Under POL-NS-01(c) the dwell runs from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the 'arrived' tap. That run does not exist, so the effective dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum - a 300-second shortfall computed in EV-GPS-00212's own derived block. POL-NS-06 therefore refunds the cancellation fee in full whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied. The traffic-advisory route in POL-NS-06(i) cannot be run: EV-ADVIS-00212-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), which makes the limb unavailable and exonerates no one; no advisory could in any case have reduced the required minimum. The driver's 'held for 7.9 minutes' figure (claim citing wait_time_min) is a trip-record measure from the marker, not the dwell the clause reads, and it does not survive POL-NS-01(c).\n\nPOL-NS-04 does not apply: the rider's 08:15:02 locating message was answered by the driver at 08:15:30, 28 seconds later and well inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) is not met regardless of the reply's content. POL-NS-03 does not change the outcome - it also yields a full refund on these facts - and it produces no driver payment: the rider named Exit A in chat, which is the single registered pickup point on this record, and the driver never moved to it, so under POL-NS-03(i) he bears the loss; the pin-ambiguity goodwill of POL-NS-03(ii) is unavailable because registered_pickup_points is 1. The rider's rider_track being equally filtered (claim 6 for the driver) is irrelevant: rider presence is not a limb of POL-NS-01, and the only clause reading rider position, POL-NS-04, fails at its own limb (b).\n\nThe driver's escalation argument does not fire. The 'arrived' marker and the GPS do not leave POL-NS-09(b) an unresolved conflict on arrival or dwell, because the clauses the dispute turns on answer which record governs: POL-NS-01(c) fixes the dwell test to the GPS and not to the marker, and POL-NS-02 fixes arrival to admissible in-radius fixes. The anti-farming check is not tripped (2 no-show terminations against 132 completed trips, 1.5%, and both limbs of POL-NS-07 must hold), no counterparty-dispute counters exist on either profile, and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) do not fire; POL-NS-09(a) and (e) do not fire because the deciding fact is carried by a clean weight-1.0 artifact. The fare line reconciles with the fee schedule - 4.00 is the greater of the STANDARD zone fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee (4.00) - so POL-NS-08(d) discloses no defect, and the money is otherwise sound.\n\nOutcome: the $4.00 cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full to the rider. No compensation is payable to the driver, because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full and POL-NS-03(i) places the loss on him. Confidence is capped at 1.0 by EV-GPS-00212, the weight-1.0 artifact that carries the deciding fact; I state it at 0.9."
